git-khronos (0.1.8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Show an available-update shortcut next to the running version. It opens
    Updates without starting a download or installer.
  * Open WSL system authorization from the app, without requiring a terminal
    command or collecting credentials in Git Khronos.
  * Explain installer refusal and show when a saved deferral requires a
    manual retry of this release.
  * Clarify working-tree totals and bulk action scope while filtering changes.
  * Identify tracked files whose own recovery snapshots exceed the discard
    budget, without modifying their working contents.

 -- Maurizio Casciano <mauriziocasciano7@gmail.com>  Sat, 28 Nov 2026 03:26:27 +0100

git-khronos (0.1.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Show a running build ID in Updates to distinguish Debian builds that
    report the same application version.
  * Keep signer diagnostics tied to the repository that requested them,
    and explain that finding the signer does not verify the key.
  * Keep keyboard navigation working during menu focus handoffs, including
    reverse Tab in the packaged Linux webview.
  * Filter the eligible files in a blocked bulk discard review and select
    only the currently shown matches without losing hidden selections.
  * Explain why bulk submodule updates are blocked and which remote reads
    may have completed when Fetch All reports a partial failure.
  * Preserve rename drafts while Git is busy and report browser or file
    manager launch failures without removing the retry action.

 -- Maurizio Casciano <mauriziocasciano7@gmail.com>  Sat, 28 Nov 2026 00:41:01 +0100

git-khronos (0.1.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Reload the window when its page renderer crashes on Linux instead of
    leaving a blank, unreachable instance.
  * Prevent a startup crash on the affected WSLg X11 path by using the
    current session's accessibility bus without disabling accessibility.
  * Show additions and deletions for unstaged changes, and give Unstaged
    Files more room when Staged Files is collapsed.
  * Review and discard all eligible unstaged files from one action. Support
    recovery for ordinary nested files on Linux without unstaging changes.
  * Offer to open the linked worktree that owns a checked-out branch
    instead of detaching the current checkout.
  * Let users add a reason when locking a linked worktree, and explain
    why its removal actions are unavailable until it is unlocked.
  * Add manual update checks and optional automatic updates with publisher
    verification. Automatic updates are off by default.
  * Copy the full commit ID from a file history row and clear clipboard
    feedback when the file history revision changes.
  * Keep large diff minimaps lightweight without changing where their
    jump buttons navigate.
  * Show invalid blame line numbers beside the input instead of offering
    to retry the last read.
  * Copy the full Git ref from branch and tag menus, even when the short
    names are ambiguous.

 -- Maurizio Casciano <mauriziocasciano7@gmail.com>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:38:17 +0100

